# Your settings for the Sakala Agent, read after agent.env and winning over it.
# install.sh writes this file once and never changes it again. Restart after editing:
#   sudo systemctl restart sakala-agent
#
# Leave the values agent.env takes from your domain alone, such as
# SAKALA_PROJECT_DOMAIN_SUFFIXES and SAKALA_PUBLIC_API_URL; names follow
# sakala-agent docs/CONFIGURATION.md.
#
# A different node limit, for example more replicas per deployment (1 to 64):
# SAKALA_MAX_REPLICAS_PER_PROJECT=8
#
# Managed PostgreSQL databases (off in this installation). Only after reading
# "Database terkelola" in docs/configuration.md, which also needs a separate
# PostgreSQL instance and SAKALA_DATABASE_DEFAULT_MAX_COUNT in api.local.env:
# SAKALA_DATABASE_DRIVER=postgres
# SAKALA_DATABASE_ADMIN_DSN=host=/var/run/postgresql user=postgres dbname=postgres
# SAKALA_DATABASE_PUBLIC_HOST=10.0.0.5
# SAKALA_DATABASE_PUBLIC_PORT=5432
